  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "NM02120",
    "sub_id": "43174",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": "1. 補考規則\n考試日期後三日內，須依校規提出補考申請，並檢附相關證明文件，且提出補考之理由需遵循學校規定內正當理由（依逢甲大學學則第26條為原則）。未到考或逾期申請者，成績以零分計算。補考日期由任課教師另行安排。\n\n2. 請假規則\n所有請假申請須透過 iLearn 系統提交。若在請假週內有評分之課堂活動或作業，學生須於兩週內（不含請假當週）補交。請注意，核准之請假僅確保出缺勤紀錄不受影響，若未於期限內補交作業，該項作業仍以零分計算。\n\n3. 遲交規則\n所有作業逾期不予受理，並以零分處理，除非學生提出有效之正當理由。",
    "course_pol_en": "1. Within three days after the exam date, students must apply for a make-up exam in accordance with university regulations and submit relevant supporting documents. The reason for requesting a make-up exam must comply with the valid grounds specified in the university regulations (based on Feng Chia University Academic Regulations, Article 26). Absentees or late applicants will receive a grade of zero. The date of the make-up exam will be arranged by the course instructor.\n2. All leave of absence requests must be submitted through iLearn. If graded in-class activities or coursework fall during the week of your absence, you will have two weeks (excluding the week of absence) to submit the work. Please note that an approved leave of absence only ensures that your attendance record will not be affected. However, if you fail to submit the coursework for that week, you will still receive a grade of zero for the assignment.\n3. Late works will not be accepted and will be marked zero as punishment unless a valid excuse is provided.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<div>學生應遵守誠信原則，避免任何形式之抄襲、代寫、作弊或資料偽造。所有作業、報告與考試必須為個人真實成果，並正確引用他人研究。違反規則者，將依校方規定懲處，以維護學術品質與公平。</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<ol>\n\t<li>Students must exhibit honesty and ethical behavior in their academic activities, avoiding plagiarism and falsification of data.</li>\n\t<li>Plagiarism: Proper citation of sources is required. Copying or using others&rsquo; work without appropriate attribution in considered plagiarism.</li>\n\t<li>Cheating: Following exam rules is mandatory. Unauthorized materials or collusion with others during exam is considered cheating.</li>\n</ol>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
